# patra_crash_repro.cyr — documents runtime crash condition
#
# When libro's full src/main.cyr (240 tests, ~1,780 lines of test code)
# includes both lib/sigil.cyr and lib/patra.cyr, the binary compiles
# (348KB on cc3 3.4.8) but crashes at runtime with SIGSEGV during
# patra operations.
#
# Proven:
#   1. sigil + patra + libro modules + minimal main = WORKS (303KB)
#   2. sigil + patra + libro modules + 50 stub test fns = WORKS (303KB)
#   3. sigil + libro modules + 240 real tests (no patra) = WORKS (266KB)
#   4. sigil + patra + libro modules + 240 real tests = CRASHES (348KB)
#
# The crash is a runtime SIGSEGV, not a compile error.
# It occurs during patra_open() or patra_exec() calls.
# The binary compiles cleanly with no warnings.
#
# Root cause: unknown. Likely cc3 codegen issue with binaries
# exceeding ~340KB or ~250 functions. Possibly:
#   - Code section overflow / bad jump targets
#   - Data section collision with heap
#   - Global variable address miscalculation at scale
#
# To reproduce:
#   1. In src/main.cyr, uncomment:
#      include "lib/patra.cyr"
#      include "src/patra_store.cyr"
#      test_group("PatraStore") and all test_patrastore_* calls
#   2. Build: cat src/main.cyr | cc3 > build/libro
#   3. Run:  ./build/libro  # crashes at PatraStore test group
#
# Filed for: Cyrius compiler investigation
# Blocked:   libro PatraStore in main test suite
# See also:  tests/patra_standalone.cyr (proves patra code is correct)
